==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed Dragon Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Manic King Dragon''' when obtained from the [[Draconian (Deadly)|Lizard Maniac]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Crazed Lizard Cat is essentially similar to the original as a ranged support unit to chip enemies with relative safety. Its above-average range of 400 means it can work against high-range threats like [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[I.M. Phace]], to name a few. In addition to high range, Crazed Dragon Cat also sports considerable bulk. Its health allows it to take some hits, ensuring that a single blow doesn't erase an entire stack. Although it may not be that fragile, meatshielding still helps tons.

This cat is also very helpful against enemies that are close ranged. Just be sure to keep the distance at a maximum, so that the enemies can't advance and hit it. When combined with King Dragon Cat or [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]], their combined DPS can quickly stack up. This strategy is great for stages like [[Revenge of Red Sky (Merciless)|Revenge of Red Sky]], which feature backliners most other units cannot outrange.

In terms of DPS, a level 30 Crazed Dragon Cat is equal to a level 20+28 [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]]. As prior to True Form this cat shares the same range as its [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]] counterpart, a high level King Dragon Cat may be worth using instead.

It also has access to the excellent [[Sigh of Relief (Combo)|Sigh of Relief]] [[Cat Combo]]. Given how powerful Research is, it may be worth adding Kaoluga to your lineup solely for the combo.

==='''True Form'''===
Manic King Dragon gains more range and attack power in true form, meaning that Manic King Dragon is now able to outrange [[Le'boin]] and his variants (excluding [[Le'Grim]]). Proper meatshielding is required, since he only outranges them by 15 (5 for [[Le'noir]] and [[Le'Behemoth]]).

It is also important to note that while Dragon Cat has a shorter cooldown than King Dragon Cat, Manic King Dragon does not have this cooldown difference. As such, it is always worth using this unit's True Form over other forms.

Unfortunately, as you advance further into the game, Manic King Dragon and its variants will be less and less favorable due to the expansive prevalence of piercing threats who can reach Manic King Dragon. Furthermore, many specialists become available late in the game who outclass Dragon variants in their respective niches.

